  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "snuoQ+DkMICKWy6Lrd69LvDFF9Q=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:22:11.166Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The demo shape recorded for this cohort is a single move repeated against whatever the lead already runs: pick one tool from their published stack, have a webhook or a hook dispatch a typed operation into Powerhouse, then delete the source record and replay it from Powerhouse. The research text is explicit about why this generalises \u2014 the demo is stack-agnostic *because the gap is*. What is being demonstrated is not a property of any one product; it is the absence of an append-only, attributed record in the place the source record lived.\n\nThat matters because these 50 leads have almost nothing in common at the tooling layer. The published stacks in the source records range across Microsoft, SAP, Salesforce, AWS and IBM at one lead, Peppol plus 200-plus in-house software products at another, an explicitly Java-and-open-source shop at a third, and \"stack not verified\" at several more. Geographically the group spans NL (13), UK (9), DK (8), ES (6), PT (5), SI (4), DE (3) and BE (1). Because the integration binds to a generic extension point rather than to the semantics of a specific product, the engineering cost of the demo is paid once and the per-lead work collapses to choosing a tool and writing one hook.\n\nThe commercial caveat is in the lead metadata rather than the demo text. Of the 50 leads carrying this finding, only three sit at priority 1, six at priority 2 and nine at priority 3; 17 are parked at \"4 \u00b7 needs OSS screen\" and 15 at \"9 \u00b7 do not pitch\". A reusable demo therefore lowers the cost of serving this cohort but does not qualify it \u2014 29 of the 50 arrived from the provisional v2 ranking tail, and the screening work is a separate gate from the build work.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (50)\n\n**1 \u00b7 parallel track**\n- Digitaal Vlaanderen (BE)\n\n**1 \u00b7 start here**\n- Scott Logic (UK \u00b7 350+)\n- Trifork (DK \u00b7 1,148 / 16 countries)\n\n**2 \u00b7 next**\n- AMIS Conclusion (NL \u00b7 opco)\n- Comtrade 360 (SI \u00b7 89 (2024))\n- Equal Experts (UK \u00b7 1,000-5,000)\n- First8 Conclusion (NL \u00b7 opco)\n- Made Tech (UK \u00b7 433)\n- TPXimpact (UK \u00b7 GBP 78.1m)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Atabix (NL)\n- INFO (info.nl) (NL)\n- Info Support (NL \u00b7 500+)\n- Novabase (PT \u00b7 not verified)\n- Organisation (Ctry)\n- SRC d.o.o. (SI \u00b7 300)\n- Softwire (UK \u00b7 not verified)\n- Xebia (NL \u00b7 7,511 global (~61% India))\n- Xpand IT (PT \u00b7 370+)\n\n**4 \u00b7 needs OSS screen**\n- Agitavit Solutions (SI)\n- BEC Financial Technologies (DK)\n- Bankdata (DK)\n- Berenschot (NL)\n- Critical Software (PT)\n- Evolutio (ES)\n- GMV (ES)\n- Halcom (SI)\n- Highberg (NL)\n- JN Data (DK)\n- M&I/Partners (NL)\n- PPI AG (DE)\n- SDC (DK)\n- Systematic (DK)\n- VASS (ES)\n- cbs Corporate Business Solutions (DE)\n- ilionx (NL)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Ayesa (incl. Ibermatica) (ES \u00b7 13,200)\n- BJSS (UK)\n- Centric (NL)\n- Critical TechWorks (PT)\n- Endava (UK)\n- GFT UK (UK)\n- Glintt (PT)\n- Indra / Minsait (ES \u00b7 62,396)\n- KMD (DK)\n- MHP (DE)\n- PinkRoccade (Healthcare / Local Gov) (NL)\n- Seidor (ES)\n- Sopra Steria Netherlands (NL)\n- Sopra Steria UK (UK)\n- twoday (DK \u00b7 2,200-3,000)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Pick one tool from their published stack and show the same move: a webhook or hook dispatching a typed operation, then delete the source record and replay it from Powerhouse. Stack-agnostic because the gap is.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:22:11.166559Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:22:11.166564Z"
    }
